>> title: Vodka Sauce
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: tomato, cream, pasta, vegetarian, stovetop
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> aka: penne alla vodka, vodka slice, pink sauce
>> servings: 6
>> time: 40 min
>> slack: narrow — the tomato paste is fried to brick red in about four minutes with thirty seconds of room; past that it burns bitter

>> step: sweat 6 min
Sweat @shallot{1%large}(minced) and @garlic{3%cloves}(minced) in @unsalted butter{3%Tbs}(45 g) over medium heat for ~{6%min}.

>> step: fry until brick red, 4 min
Fry @tomato paste{1/4%cup}(65 g) and @red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)aromatics{} for ~{4%min}, until brick red.

>> step: reduce by half
Reduce @vodka{1/3%cup}(80 mL) into @&(~1)paste{} by half.

>> step: simmer 15 min
Simmer @&(~1)base{} with @crushed tomatoes{28%oz}(800 g) and @kosher salt{1%tsp} for ~{15%min}.

>> step: finish off heat
Finish @&(~1)sauce{} off the heat with @heavy cream{3/4%cup}(180 mL), @grated Parmigiano-Reggiano{1/2%cup}(50 g), and @fresh basil{6%leaves}(torn).
